# Body framing: CL must be exactly 0 on the proxy path, so a body is refused, but a trailing
# request line with NO Content-Length is re-parsed as a second request (keep-alive only).
CTL GET /hello.txt                                  -> 200 body=ALPHA
POST /api?cmd=whoami with CL=24 and a body          -> 400 Bad Request, no upstream connection
GET /api?cmd=id, keep-alive, then a bare second line -> 400 (first) AND a second upstream hit
UPSTREAM (last two): LINE=b'GET /exec  HTTP/1.1' TOKS=4  (x2)
# The 400 does not close the connection, so the leftover line is parsed and proxied.
# Source: line 67 gate (!headers["content-length"].empty() && ...[0]!="0") -> 400.
